"A buster shot's +0x4C (the third kind's type 0, each engine's own object: BN4's 0x0800B590 spawns it through 0x080CD45A, BN6's twin 0x0800FAAC through 0x080C686E): its kind's row in its game's table of the shots' kinds, set as it is made (BN4 0x080CD354-0x080CD360: its +4 times 9 added to 0x080CD2A8), BN4's rows 9 bytes, BN6's 12 at 0x080C64E8 (its 9 and three of padding), and read by its hit (BN4's ldr r3,[r5,#0x4c] at 0x080CD440 into 0x08009DC4, BN6's at 0x080C6818, 0x080C6838 and 0x080C6854 into 0x0800CC0A). Read as the same where each is its own game's row of the same kind and the two rows hold the same 9 bytes (kind 3, GutsSoul's rapid buster's shots, 04 05 00 00 05 ff ff 01 ff in both; kinds 2, 4 and 5 differ and are compared as they are: tools/xdiff_bn4.py shot_row); bn4_soul_guts_rapid at t168"
